# Sum nested arrays - recursion

## Description

You are given a nested array of integers. Your task is to return the sum of all the integers in the array, including those in nested arrays.
The array can be nested to any depth, and it may contain other arrays as well as integers. The integers can be positive or negative.

## Example

```javascript
sumNestedArray([1, 2, [3, 4], [5, [6, 7]]]); // returns 28
sumNestedArray([1, 2, [3, 4], [5, [6, -7]]]); // returns 10
sumNestedArray([1, 2, [3, 4], [5, [6, -7]], -8]); // returns 2
```

## Constraints

- The input array will always be a valid nested array of integers.
- The input array will not be empty.
- The integers in the array can be positive or negative.

## Task

Write a function `sumNestedArray(arr)` that takes a nested array of integers as input and returns the sum of all the integers in the array, including those in nested arrays.
